  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1210 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nTuesday night through Sunday:\n\nSynopsis: The slow-moving cold front approaching during the short \nterm period will continue into the area on Wednesday, with global \nforecast guidance beginning to hint at its northward return as a \nwarm front through the second half of the work week. Above normal \ntemperatures and muggy conditions are thus becoming favored into \nnext weekend, though it remains uncertain if the combined heat and \nhumidity will reach the very uncomfortable levels anticipated during \nthe short term period. This will be a trend to monitor over coming \nforecasts. Given the lingering surface front & still warm/muggy \nconditions, additional periods of showers and storms are anticipated \nthrough at least the beginning of next weekend. Whether or not any \nstorms could be strong/severe remains uncertain, with trends being \nmonitored through the first half of this week. While not yet \nconclusive across all global guidance, some solutions hint that \nbuilding high pressure over the Quebec-Ontario vicinity could begin \nushering in drier air by the second half of next weekend. If these \nsignals were to verify, a more seasonable pattern change would be in \nstore for Sunday & just beyond the current long term period.  \n\nQuigley",
